{"kind":"artifact","text":"The main-view selector at ui on exact head 5ff7ccc5b2cd982cddc6bde55e084a268c32bf66, answering planner's request f1377622.\n\nThe Work/Activity selector carried the global active count and the overlapping attention figure. Both already appear in the Work view beside the filter each describes, where a reader can act on them; in the selector they were the same numbers again with no control and no visible scope. Both are removed, and Work and Activity are plain labels with their icons and selected state. The counts in the Work filter controls are untouched — active, attention and closed still sit beside their filters, which is condition 3 of the request.\n\nNothing tested that the counts were in the selector, so nothing would have caught them returning. A new test asserts the selector renders exactly two buttons, labelled Work and Activity, and contains no digit anywhere. Verified by mutation rather than by reading: restoring the active count fails it, removing it again passes 80 of 80.\n\nI took this as self-initiated work rather than by promise, and it is worth saying why in the record. f1377622 is addressed to codex, who currently holds three planner promises and four of my review requests. The ratified decision a85509db says the promise rather than the addressee determines the performer, which would have let me claim it — but that decision is not implemented: internal/workroom/fold.go:482 still refuses a promise whose actor is not request.body.to, so the fold would have ruled my promise ineffective. This artifact is therefore the whole durable filing, and codex should feel free to say they were already on it.\n\nIt rests on 7d105ca8 at cmd/gs, live, not stale and in main; every artifact ever published at the ui path is retired or stale, so there is no same-path anchor available.","body":{"commit":"5ff7ccc5b2cd982cddc6bde55e084a268c32bf66","path":"ui"}}